{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he looked, and behold, a well in the field.</b> It chanced to him that he saw three flocks of sheep lying beside it — a sign that there are three to whom a woman chanced to come at a well, and they are Isaac, Jacob, and Moses, because a woman is likened to a well, as it says (Proverbs 5:15), ״שְׁתֵה מַיִם מִבּוֹרֶךָ וְנֹזְלִים מִתּוֹךְ בְּאֵרֶךָ״. And we may say further that three flocks of sheep were lying upon it is a hint that there are three partners in a person, and therefore it chanced to him that three flocks of sheep drank from the well — so the three partners that are in a person draw from there to give drink to all who are born. 'And a great stone was upon the mouth of the well' — for the modest woman is called ״גַּן נָעוּל מַעְיָן חָתוּם״ (Song of Songs 4:12), as though sealed with a stone, and it is not opened except at the time of procreation, and after this they return the stone to its place — not to make use of this well except at the time of need for the maintenance of the species." "And the Sages of blessed memory interpreted (Genesis Rabbah 70:9) the matter of the well in several different ways: some say, 'and behold, a well' — this is the Temple; and some say, this is Sinai, etc. And according to all of them, the verses do not depart from their plain sense; rather, their intent is to say that this is why the matter of the well and the shepherds chanced to Jacob — so that there would be a sign placed in his hand concerning the future. And in this matter the Sages disagreed about what the matter hints at."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:00.375818500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}